{"name":"Eaves","hex":"#cecdad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Eaves","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A hamlet in Woodplumpton parish, city of Preston district, Lancashire, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Eaves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eaves","blocks":[{"text":"The eaves are the edges of the roof which overhang the face of a wall and, normally, project beyond the side of a building. The eaves form an overhang to throw water clear of the walls and may be highly decorated as part of an architectural style, such as the Chinese dougong bracket systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/F09.St.-L%C3%A9onard-de-Noblat.0025.JPG/330px-F09.St.-L%C3%A9onard-de-Noblat.0025.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eaves","wikidata":"Q163972"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Italianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg/500px-Italianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Italianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg/1280px-Italianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Italianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg/500px-Italianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Italianate eaves with decorative support brackets","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalianate_eave_with_brackets.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons